<%# A recording handed over, in whichever form it is in: the file a recorder
   exported, or the words themselves.

   TWO WAYS IN BECAUSE THE RECORDINGS ARRIVE TWO WAYS. A meeting recorder
   writes a file; Voice Memos reads the whole thing back as one unbroken line
   on screen with nowhere to save it, and the only way to upload that was to
   paste it into a text editor, save it, and come back here for the file. Both
   are read by the same parser — see Transcripts::Intake.

   `id` suffixes every input, because this partial appears twice on an
   application: once on its own panel, once inside the form that logs a beat.
   `notes` is the beats it can be tied to, and nil where the form is already
   making the one it belongs to. %>
<div class="transcript-intake">
  <%# The box IS the instruction. A file input on its own says you may pick a
     file and says nothing at all about dropping one, which is the gesture
     everybody tries first. The input stays underneath, so this degrades to a
     plain file picker if the script never runs. %>
  <div class="drop" data-drop>
    <p class="drop-say"><strong>Drop a transcript here</strong></p>
    <%= label_tag "transcript_file_#{id}", "or choose a file" %>
    <%= file_field_tag "job_transcript[file]", accept: ".txt,.vtt,.srt,text/plain",
          id: "transcript_file_#{id}" %>
    <p class="drop-got" data-drop-got></p>
    <span class="field-hint">
      A recorder's export — captions with timestamps, plain
      <code>Name: what they said</code> lines, or one unbroken wall of text
      with no names in it at all.
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="form-field transcript-paste">
    <%= label_tag "transcript_text_#{id}", "or paste the words" %>
    <%= text_area_tag "job_transcript[text]", nil, rows: 3, id: "transcript_text_#{id}",
          placeholder: "Thanks for making the time today. Happy to be here…" %>
    <span class="field-hint">
      Straight out of Voice Memos or a phone transcription, one line and all
      of it. It is kept as a text file and read exactly like one.
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="split-fields">
    <div class="form-field">
      <%= label_tag "transcript_title_#{id}", "What it was" %>
      <%= text_field_tag "job_transcript[title]", nil, id: "transcript_title_#{id}",
            placeholder: "Hiring manager interview" %>
    </div>

    <% if notes %>
      <div class="form-field">
        <%= label_tag "transcript_note_#{id}", "Against which beat" %>
        <%= select_tag "job_transcript[job_note_id]",
              options_for_select(notes.map { |note|
                ["#{note.tag_label} · #{note.occurred_at.strftime('%b %-d')}", note.id]
              }),
              include_blank: "Not tied to one", id: "transcript_note_#{id}" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
